  <text id="title" x="58" y="40" width="940" height="46" font="heading" size="30" color="ink" wrap="false">Low-connectivity field operations</text>
  <text id="subtitle" x="58" y="86" width="1088" height="30" font="body" size="16" color="muted">A procurement-grade platform for Nigeria must continue to function when teams leave office connectivity and move into inspection, boundary, and corridor environments.</text>
  <shape id="shot-frame" type="rect" x="58" y="136" width="646" height="404" fill="paper" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1" shadow="true"/>
  <image id="field-shot" src="https://private-us-east-1.manuscdn.com/sessionFile/i7Z8860JB409ZwkKDDtAu7/sandbox/slides_resource_ilxvirqgh4ifccy9plf8t-99b462a3-e2b-prod-us2_1784582081256_na1fn_L2hvbWUvdWJ1bnR1L2lkbHJfcHRzX21vYmlsZS9wcmVzZW50YXRpb25fYXNzZXRzL2ZpZWxkX3NlZWRlZF92MQ.png?x-oss-process=image/resize,w_1560,h_1560/format,webp&Expires=1786752000&__&Key-Pair-Id=K2QY5QTL8JSY6C&Signature=MEYCIQDEqNrgoGRVG~l~38GadujC73~jyKA7lGaDCHtTmnUvHQIhAIZzcRNhNjxeXAmeATIjhNftoV9jA1GDeqKG7LzAmgRS" x="70" y="160" width="622" height="356" fit="cover"/>
  <text id="shot-label" x="70" y="144" width="622" height="14" font="micro" size="11" color="muted" align="center" wrap="false">Real web screenshot • field mission workflow and operational continuity layer</text>
  <shape id="right-card" type="rect" x="736" y="136" width="486" height="404" fill="mist" stroke="hairline" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="right-title" x="762" y="164" width="434" height="26" font="body" size="20" color="ink"><p><strong>Why this matters operationally</strong></p></text>
  <text id="right-copy" x="762" y="202" width="434" height="310" font="body" size="17" color="ink" line-height="1.34">
    <p>Inspectors, survey support teams, land officers, and corridor reviewers do not always work with stable connectivity. The platform therefore supports continuity before, during, and after network failure.</p>
    <p space-before="14"><strong>Key controls include:</strong></p>
    <p space-before="10">• Offline persistence for field actions and evidence context.</p>
    <p>• Replay and reconciliation when service returns.</p>
    <p>• Encrypted local audit-package cache for inspectors.</p>
    <p>• Biometric unlock for protected offline evidence access.</p>
    <p>• Geofence-aware alerts and offline geofence replay where location events matter.</p>
    <p space-before="14">For procurement teams, this means service continuity is designed into the operating model instead of being left to best effort.</p>
  </text>
  <shape id="bottom-band" type="rect" x="58" y="566" width="1164" height="56" fill="#ECFDF5" stroke="#BBF7D0" stroke-width="1"/>
  <text id="bottom-copy" x="82" y="584" width="1116" height="18" font="body" size="17" color="ink" align="center" wrap="false">The field layer helps state agencies and delivery partners keep evidence, decisions, and inspections moving even when connectivity is uneven.</text>
